When a checkbox or radio button keeps its native appearance, Ladybird
takes the bottom of its border box as its baseline, and one with
“appearance: none” gets the ordinary synthesized baseline. Blink does
the same: LayoutTheme::AdjustCheckboxStyle() and AdjustRadioStyle()
set InlineBlockBaselineEdge::kBorderBox, and “appearance: none”
skips those adjustments. WebKit’s RenderTheme::baselinePosition() returns
the box’s borderBoxHeight() for a themed control. And Gecko’s
nsCheckboxRadioFrame::GetNaturalBaselineBOffset() puts the baseline at
the block-end edge, inset by the theme’s border width, but only with
native appearance.
